/maelstrom/demo/go@v0.0.0-20260710121306-480a8197026d\n```\n\nThen write main.go, build, and run the test command. Note the test command uses `--bin /usr/local/bin/maelstrom-rename` with `MAELSTROM_RENAME_BIN=/work/node`. Let's run it.\n\nNote: maelstrom test needs a Java runtime? Maelstrom is a Clojure program; requires java. It's said maelstrom 0.2.4 is installed as `maelstrom` command, so presumably java is available. Let's test.\n\nLet me also double check stderr logging: fine.\n\nLet's start.\n\nPotential issue: writing to stdout must be exactly the framed JSON; library does that.\n\nLet me do the work.\n\nAlso consider: should ticket be a string? \"A ticket can be any JSON value: a string, a number, an array.\" So string is fine.\n\nPlan:\n1. `go mod init node && go get ...`\n2. Write main.go\n3. `go build -o node .`\n4. Run the maelstrom test command (30s time limit + setup; may take ~1 min). Use timeout 600? The test with time-limit 30 takes maybe 60-90 seconds. Set timeout 300.\n\nLet's go. First, check environment.", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"arguments": {"command": "ls -la /work && go version && which maelstrom java"}, "arguments_error": null, "id": "call_01a20413dcdb7cd39a52736e", "name": "shell"}, {"arguments": {"command": "ls /usr/local/bin/ && cat /usr/local/bin/maelstrom-rename 2>/dev/null | head -50"}, "arguments_error": null, "id": "call_01a20413dd2870a38773f053", "name": "shell"}], "usage": {"input_tokens": 1174, "output_tokens": 1298}}}
