{"seq": 18, "type": "assistant_message", "ts": "2026-11-22T16:26:50.256075+00:00", "payload": {"reasoning": "Good. Now write main.go. I'll make the ticket format: `<nodeID>-<session>-<counter>`. Actually to make it look like the example \"n3-204\", maybe simpler: `n3-204` style is just nodeID-counter. Including a session token makes it longer but safe. Let me keep it simple but robust.\n\nLet me write it.", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"arguments": {"content": "// Command node implements a box-office machine that issues tickets with\n// globally unique numbers.\n//\n// Every ticket must be unique across the whole cluster, and every request must\n// be answered immediately, even when the node is partitioned away from all its\n// peers. Those two requirements together rule out any coordination: instead\n// each node mints ticket numbers locally out of three parts that cannot\n// collide:\n//\n//   - the node's own ID, which Maelstrom guarantees is distinct per machine\n//     (n1, n2, ...),\n//   - a random per-process token, so that even a restarted process whose\n//     counter starts over cannot re-issue a ticket it already handed out,\n//   - a monotonically increasing counter.\n//\n// The ticket is just a string like \"n3-9f2c1a7b-204\"; clients treat it as an\n// opaque value.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"crypto/rand\"\n\t\"encoding/hex\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"sync/atomic\"\n\n\tmaelstrom \"github.com/jepsen-io/maelstrom/demo/go\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n\tn := maelstrom.NewNode()\n\n\t// Random token for this process incarnation. If the process were ever\n\t// killed and restarted, the counter would start over, but this token\n\t// changes too, so old tickets can never be repeated.\n\tvar seed [8]byte\n\tif _, err := rand.Read(seed[:]); err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(fmt.Sprintf(\"node: cannot read random seed: %v\", err))\n\t}\n\tincarnation := hex.EncodeToString(seed[:])\n\n\tvar counter atomic.Uint64\n\n\tn.Handle(\"issue\", func(msg maelstrom.Message) error {\n\t\tticket := fmt.Sprintf(\"%s-%s-%d\", n.ID(), incarnation, counter.Add(1))\n\t\treturn n.Reply(msg, map[string]any{\n\t\t\t\"type\":   \"issued\",\n\t\t\t\"ticket\": ticket,\n\t\t})\n\t})\n\n\tif err := n.Run(); err != nil {\n\t\tpanic(err)\n\t}\n}\n", "path": "/work/main.go"}, "arguments_error": null, "id": "call_01a20414edf678e381d7a5b7", "name": "write_file"}], "usage": {"input_tokens": 21518, "output_tokens": 525}}}
